Ability: Range
The simplest measurement, simply defined as the maximum minus the minimum.

Statistical process control emphasizes small sets of numbers, so range is frequently useful.

Example: Range

  Given the data values:
  | 3 | 10 | 16 | 1 | 5 | 14 | 11 | 6|
  Then the maximum value is "16"
  And the minimum value is "1"
  And the range is "15"

  Given the data values:
  | -1 | 0 | 1 |
  Then the maximum value is "1"
  And the minimum value is "-1"
  And the range is "2"

  Given the data values:
  | 100 |
  Then the maximum value is "100"
  And the minimum value is "100"
  And the range is "0"

  Given the data values:
  | -1 | -2 | -3 | -4 | -5 |
  Then the maximum value is "-1"
  And the minimum value is "-5"
  And the range is "4"
